                                               <figcaption>
<p>Box diagram of the local eddy energetics in the cyclone frame of reference. The boxes labeled <i>DA<sub>E</sub></i>/<i>Dt</i> and <i>DK<sub>E</sub></i>/<i>Dt</i> represent the tendencies of EAPE and EKE, respectively. The arrows labeled <i>G</i>(<i>A<sub>E</sub></i>), <i>D</i>(<i>K<sub>E</sub></i>), and <i>B</i>(<i>K<sub>E</sub></i>) represent the generation of EAPE, the dissipation of EKE, and the boundary flux of EKE in the eddy energy equations [Eqs. <a id="ref_E15" href="#E15">(15)</a> and <a id="ref_E16" href="#E16">(16)</a>]. The arrow labeled <i>C</i>(*, *) represents the energy conversion terms, while the wavy arrows labeled <i>A</i>(<i>A<sub>E</sub></i>) and <i>A</i>(<i>K<sub>E</sub></i>) represent the energy advection by the background flow relative to the cyclone movement.</p></figcaption>
                                           
