<p>(a) The vertically integrated EAPE tendency (<i>DA<sub>E</sub></i>/<i>Dt</i>; black bar; left <i>y</i> axis) derived from EAPE budget [Eq. <a id="ref_E16" href="#E16">(16)</a>], consisting of EAPE generation [<i>G</i>(<i>A<sub>E</sub></i>); red bar; right <i>y</i> axis], EAPE conversion from background flow [<i>C</i>(<i>A<sub>I</sub></i>, <i>A<sub>E</sub></i>); yellow bar; right <i>y</i> axis], baroclinic energy conversion from EKE to EAPE [−<i>C</i>(<i>A<sub>E</sub></i>, <i>K<sub>E</sub></i>); green bar; right <i>y</i> axis], EAPE advection [<i>A</i>(<i>A<sub>E</sub></i>); blue bar; right <i>y</i> axis], and residual (pink bar; right <i>y</i> axis). (b) As in (a), but for the EKE tendency (<i>DK<sub>E</sub></i>/<i>Dt</i>; black bar) derived from EKE budget [Eq. <a id="ref_E15" href="#E15">(15)</a>], consisting of boundary flux [<i>B</i>(<i>K<sub>E</sub></i>); red bar], dissipation [<i>D</i>(<i>K<sub>E</sub></i>); orange bar], EKE conversion from background flow [<i>C</i>(<i>K<sub>I</sub></i>, <i>K<sub>E</sub></i>); yellow bar], baroclinic energy conversion from EAPE to EKE [<i>C</i>(<i>A<sub>E</sub></i>, <i>K<sub>E</sub></i>); green bar], EKE advection [<i>A</i>(<i>K<sub>E</sub></i>); blue bar], and residual (pink bar). All values are averaged within a 500-km radius around the TC center. Solid bars and hatched bars indicate TC and ET phases, respectively. Note that the ranges of the left and right <i>y</i> axes differ.</p></figcaption>
                                           
