                        <span class="caption text-caption color-text-primary">
                            <b><sc>Fig</sc>. 4.</b>
                            
<p>850-hPa geopotential height anomaly (shading; gpm), integrated water vapor transport (IVT) (vectors; &gt;300 kg m<sup>−1</sup> s<sup>−1</sup>), 250-hPa geopotential height (contours; gpm) at (a) 1800 UTC 10 Oct, (c) 1200 UTC 11 Oct, (e) 0600 UTC 12 Oct, and (g) 0000 UTC 13 Oct 2019. The boundary of the western North Pacific high is highlighted by a bold 5880-gpm contour. (b),(d),(f),(h) As in (a), (c), (e), and (g), but for 850-hPa equivalent potential temperature (shading; K), and the horizontal gradient of 850-hPa equivalent potential temperature [contours; for positive values starting from 6 K (100 km)<sup>−1</sup> with a 1 K (100 km)<sup>−1</sup> interval]. The red × in the (a), (c), (e), and (g) marks the TC center.</p>
                            
