                    <li data-value="{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fig1&quot;,&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fig1_0&quot;,&quot;imageUris&quot;:[&quot;/view/journals/atsc/83/9/full-JAS-D-26-0015.1-f1.jpg&quot;],&quot;header&quot;:&quot;&lt;sc&gt;Fig&lt;\/sc&gt;. 1.&quot;,&quot;footer&quot;:&quot;&lt;caption encoding-type=\&quot;nlm\&quot; ifp-element-xpath=\&quot;/*[local-name() = 'figure' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']/*[local-name() = 'caption' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Box diagram of the local eddy energetics in the cyclone frame of reference. The boxes labeled &lt;i&gt;DA&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;/&lt;i&gt;Dt&lt;\/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;DK&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;/&lt;i&gt;Dt&lt;\/i&gt; represent the tendencies of EAPE and EKE, respectively. The arrows labeled &lt;i&gt;G&lt;\/i&gt;(&lt;i&gt;A&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;), &lt;i&gt;D&lt;\/i&gt;(&lt;i&gt;K&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;), and &lt;i&gt;B&lt;\/i&gt;(&lt;i&gt;K&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;) represent the generation of EAPE, the dissipation of EKE, and the boundary flux of EKE in the eddy energy equations [Eqs. &lt;a href=\&quot;#E15\&quot; id=\&quot;ref_E15\&quot;&gt;(15)&lt;\/a&gt; and &lt;a href=\&quot;#E16\&quot; id=\&quot;ref_E16\&quot;&gt;(16)&lt;\/a&gt;]. The arrow labeled &lt;i&gt;C&lt;\/i&gt;(*, *) represents the energy conversion terms, while the wavy arrows labeled &lt;i&gt;A&lt;\/i&gt;(&lt;i&gt;A&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;) and &lt;i&gt;A&lt;\/i&gt;(&lt;i&gt;K&lt;sub&gt;E&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;) represent the energy advection by the background flow relative to the cyclone movement.&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;\/caption&gt;&quot;,&quot;altText&quot;:&quot;&lt;caption encoding-type=\&quot;nlm\&quot; ifp-element-xpath=\&quot;/*[local-name() = 'figure' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']/*[local-name() = 'caption' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']