<p>(a) Track of TC Hagibis (2019) at 6-h intervals. (b) CPS diagram of 900–600-hPa thermal wind <inline-formula id="IE17" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM17"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></math></inline-formula> and thermal symmetry <i>B</i> for TC Hagibis (2019). (c) As in (b), but for 900–600-hPa thermal wind <inline-formula id="IE18" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM18"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></math></inline-formula> and 600–300-hPa thermal wind <inline-formula id="IE19" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM19"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup></mrow></math></inline-formula>. Red, orange, green, and blue dots indicate the beginning of the cyclone life cycle as a tropical storm, ET onset, ET completion, and the end of the JMA best track record, respectively.</p></figcaption>
                                           
