                        </span>

                        <span class="caption text-caption color-text-primary">
                            <b><sc>Fig</sc>. 3.</b>
                            
<p>(a) Track of TC Hagibis (2019) at 6-h intervals. (b) CPS diagram of 900–600-hPa thermal wind <inline-formula id="IE17" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM17"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></math></inline-formula> and thermal symmetry <i>B</i> for TC Hagibis (2019). (c) As in (b), but for 900–600-hPa thermal wind <inline-formula id="IE18" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM18"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></math></inline-formula> and 600–300-hPa thermal wind <inline-formula id="IE19" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM19"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup></mrow></math></inline-formula>. Red, orange, green, and blue dots indicate the beginning of the cyclone life cycle as a tropical storm, ET onset, ET completion, and the end of the JMA best track record, respectively.</p>
                            
                        </span>


                    </div>
                
            
                
                    <div class="figure splide__slide has-caption">

                      <ul class="actions color-primary">
                            <li><a target="_blank" href="/view/journals/atsc/83/9/full-JAS-D-26-0015.1-f4.jpg" class="ico-image-file"><span>View raw image</span></a></li>
<!--                            <li><a class="ico-powerpoint" href="#"><span><t:region key="view.image-gallery.download-powerpoint-text">Download Powerpoint Slide</t:region></span></a></li> -->

                        </ul>

                        <span class="primary-img" style="background:url(/view/journals/atsc/83/9/full-JAS-D-26-0015.1-f4.jpg)">
                           <!-- <img src="${var:currentFullImageUri}" /> -->
                        </span>

                        <span class="caption text-caption color-text-primary">
                            <b><sc>Fig</sc>. 4.</b>
                            
<p>850-hPa geopotential height anomaly (shading; gpm), integrated water vapor transport (IVT) (vectors; &gt;300 kg m<sup>−1</sup> s<sup>−1</sup>), 250-hPa geopotential height (contours; gpm) at (a) 1800 UTC 10 Oct, (c) 1200 UTC 11 Oct, (e) 0600 UTC 12 Oct, and (g) 0000 UTC 13 Oct 2019. The boundary of the western North Pacific high is highlighted by a bold 5880-gpm contour. (b),(d),(f),(h) As in (a), (c), (e), and (g), but for 850-hPa equivalent potential temperature (shading; K), and the horizontal gradient of 850-hPa equivalent potential temperature [contours; for positive values starting from 6 K (100 km)<sup>−1</sup> with a 1 K (100 km)<sup>−1</sup> interval]. The red × in the (a), (c), (e), and (g) marks the TC center.</p>
                            
                        </span>


                    </div>
                
            
                
