<p>As in <a id="ref_fig9" href="#fig9">Fig. 9</a>, but for (a),(d) vertically integrated <i>C</i>(<i>A<sub>I</sub></i>, <i>A<sub>E</sub></i>) (W m<sup>−2</sup>), (b) vertical component of vertically integrated <i>C</i>(<i>A<sub>I</sub></i>, <i>A<sub>E</sub></i>) (shading; W m<sup>−2</sup>) and vertically averaged <i>p</i>-velocity anomaly (contours; with a 0.1 Pa s<sup>−1</sup> interval), (c) vertically averaged vertical eddy heat flux (contours; with a 1 K Pa s<sup>−1</sup> interval) and vertically averaged vertical (<inline-formula id="IE21" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM21"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></math></inline-formula>) gradient (shading; 10<sup>−4</sup> K Pa<sup>−1</sup>), (e) meridional component of vertically integrated <i>C</i>(<i>A<sub>I</sub></i>, <i>A<sub>E</sub></i>) (shading; W m<sup>−2</sup>) and vertically averaged horizontal wind anomaly (vectors; m s<sup>−1</sup>), and (f) vertically averaged meridional eddy heat flux (contours; with a 30 K m s<sup>−1</sup> interval) and vertically averaged meridional (<inline-formula id="IE22" xmlns:ifp="http://www.ifactory.com/press"><math display="inline" id="IM22"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></math></inline-formula>) gradient (shading; 10<sup>−6</sup> K m<sup>−1</sup>).</p>
                            
